    <h3><ins>Chicken Chow Mein</ins></h3>
    
    <img src="Chicken-Chow-Mein-1.jpg" alt="chiken chowmain" width="300">

    <p>Chicken Chow Mein is a delicious Chinese dish made with stir-fried noodles, chicken, and fresh vegetables. It is cooked on high heat with soy sauce and other spices. It has a slightly spicy and very tasty flavor that everyone loves.</p>
    
    <h3><ins>Ingredients </ins></h3>
    
    <ul>
      <li>chicken breast</li>
      <li>noodles</li>
      <li>1 onion</li>
      <li>1 capsicum</li>
      <li>1 carrot </li>
      <li>1 cabbage </li>
      <li>1 tbsp soy sauce</li>
      <li>1 tbsp chili sauce</li>
      <li>1 tbsp vinegar </li>
      <li>1 oil </li>
      <li>1 tbsp ginger garlic paste</li>
      <li>salt to taste</li>
      <li>black pepper to taste</li>
    </ul>
    
    <h3><ins>Instructions </ins></h3>
    
    <ol>
      <li>noodles Boil water in a large pot. Add noodles and cook for 5-6 minutes. Drain the water and rinse with cold water. <li>Add 1 tsp oil and toss so they don't stick together.</li>
      <li>Heat oil in a wok or large pan on high heat.<li> Add ginger garlic paste and fry for 30 seconds. </li>
      <li>Add chicken strips. Cook until fully cooked, about 4-5 minutes.</li>
        <li>Add onion, capsicum, carrot, and cabbage. Stir-fry on high heat for 5 minutes.</li></li>
      <li>Add soy sauce, chili sauce, vinegar, salt and black pepper. Mix well</li>
      <li>Add boiled noodles. Toss everything together for 2 minutes.</li>
    </ol>
